+[0m
+Implemented video-based frame processing.
+
+**Changes**
+- Refactored the agent CLI from `--frames <directory>` to `--frame <video>`.
+- Added optional `--frame-output <directory>` to preserve extracted PNGs.
+- Added the standalone `video-frames` Rust binary:
+  ```bash
+  video-frames --frame ./recording.mp4 --output ./video-frames
+  ```
+- Added reusable `extract_video_frames` library API.
+- Frames are written as ordered files:
+  ```text
+  frame-0000000000.png
+  frame-0000000001.png
+  ```
+- Added `FrameSequence` for sequential, frame-by-frame policy processing.
+- Temporary frames are automatically removed unless `--frame-output` is supplied.
+- Added tests and updated `README.md` and `QUICKSTART.md`.
+
+**Agent Usage**
+```bash
+computeruse agent \
+  --frame ./recording.mp4 \
+  --instructions ./gui-steps.txt \
+  --trace ./trajectory.jsonl
+```
+
+FFmpeg must be installed and available on `PATH`. Missing FFmpeg now produces an actionable error.
+
+**Verification**
+- `cargo fmt --check` passed.
+- `cargo test` passed, 22 tests.
+- `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.
+- Both CLI help interfaces were validated.
